{"purpose":"Declare the EKA Standard version this project implements, and record the canonical location of the standard, so consumers and agents know which standard applies without cloning the specification repository.","content":"EKA Standard 1.0.0 is the canonical conceptual model for engineering knowledge: the definition of Artifact, Identity, State, knowledge taxonomies, the layer architecture, and exchange contracts between systems. It defines: 16 architectural principles (P1-P16); a three-layer architecture (Knowledge Layer, Operating Layer, Exchange Layer); the Identity model (Namespace, Type, ID, InstanceVersion); the State Taxonomy (Content, Execution, Planning, Container, Existence, and Note state domains); five Engineering Domains (Discovery -\u003e Architecture -\u003e Planning -\u003e Execution -\u003e Operations, strata 1-5); 12 Knowledge Dimensions; 27 canonical tokens; 7 relationship types; and 14 Conformance Rules (R0-R13). Canonical source: repository github.com/maleolabs/eka-standard — the root file EKA (compact consumer summary) and the specification/ directory (detailed normative text). This CKO records the standard the eka project conforms to; the eka-standard repository is the authoritative source of the standard itself."}